  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the AI System**\n\nI\'ve taken a look at the `gemini-api` skill file. The initial model for text tasks is set as `gemini-3.5-flash`. Now, my focus is on how to build a real-time AI meeting system, specifically targeting the \"\353\214\200\353\252\250\354\202\260 \355\230\270\355\205\224\" (Daemosan Hotel). It seems like the core concept is quite well-defined.\n\n\n**Developing the Interface**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the UI elements. I\'m leveraging Web Speech API for real-time STT. The front-end will be a React single-page application built with Next.js App Router, using Tailwind for design, and incorporating Inter and JetBrains Mono fonts along with Lucide icons. I\'m working on the sidebar, which will manage the meeting history and attendees, and the main content, including the header for the meeting title and a system status bar. The core of the design includes a timeline for confirmed text blocks, each block being editable and including speaker selection.\n\n\n**Refining the UI Components**\n\nI\'m now diving into the specific UI components, including the textarea block with a delete button, and a bottom real-time preview showing interim speech results. I\'m focusing on the footer with export and reset functions, plus the exciting AI summary feature. My plan is to create a Next.js server-side Gemini API route for summarizing transcripts, extracting key tasks, and formatting summaries to leverage that sweet \"AI\" synergy. I also intend to implement some exception handling for Web Speech API to provide a more reliable user experience!\n\n\n**Implementing Error Handling**\n\nI\'m now focusing on critical user experience improvements. I\'m adding `onerror` handlers with automatic recovery attempts or error alerts for network drops. I\'ll also implement a 30-second no-speech detection warning. To ensure data persistence, I\'m working on debounced auto-saves to LocalStorage for the current meeting under the key \"current_meeting.\" I\'ve also pivoted to confirm the font setups, looking at `app/layout.tsx` to integrate fonts properly! Finally, I\'m updating `metadata.json` for name customization as well.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will update the `metadata.json` file to name the application \"\353\214\200\353\252\250\354\202\260 \355\230\270\355\205\224 \354\213\244\354\213\234\352\260\204 AI \355\232\214\354\235\230\353\241\235 \354\213\234\354\212\244\355\205\234\", provide a brief description, add the required `\"microphone\"` frame permission, and maintain the `\"MAJOR_CAPABILITY_SERVER_SIDE_GEMINI_API\"` capability."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 5
      nanos: 550336288
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
