  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Firebase Rules**\n\nI\'m working on the `firestore.rules` for the Firebase integration. I\'ve started with the necessary structure, including setting `rules_version = \'2\';` and the service as `cloud.firestore`. Now, I\'m diving into the actual rules we need for Phase 2, 3, and 4. I\'m exploring the specific requirements of those phases to ensure proper access control.\n\n\n**Implementing Global Rules**\n\nI\'ve established a global safety net with `allow read, write: if false;`, ensuring strict initial access control. I\'m building reusable helper functions. `isValidId()` is fleshed out to validate strings, sizes, and regex patterns. I\'m implementing `isSignedIn()` and `isVerified()`, the latter enforcing `request.auth.token.email_verified == true` for standard write operations. This adheres to our verification mandate. Next is `incoming()`.\n\n\n**Defining Data Validation**\n\nI\'m now focusing on data validation within the Firebase Rules. I\'ve started designing specific functions, starting with `isValidUser(data)`, `isValidMeeting(data)`, and `isValidTranscriptItem(data)`. Each function checks required fields, data types, and size constraints. I am now looking at the rules for `/users/{userId}` directories.\n\n\n"
  }
}
